       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is well above the 200 mg/day maximum, and I know of no indication that supports it. At that dose, a 70 kg patient with normal organ function faces a real risk of serious harm. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical rationale, so I don't have enough to override that concern.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Give me the dose and I'll enter it now, for example 100 mg or 200 mg once daily.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think a dose this high is warranted, discuss it with the attending and a clinical pharmacist. Then tell me the indication and rationale, and I'll enter it with a note that it was reviewed and flagged for pharmacy verification.\n- **Check for a different intent.** Sertraline may not be the intended drug, or the order may have been meant as a different dose, such as 100 mg.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
